  "gameDescriptionHtml": "\nFrom the illustrators behind the comedy horror webtoon <i>Erma, Erma: The Game</i> is a point-and-click adventure game, where you play as the titular character Erma. As your science fair project goes explosively awry, you must find the pieces that have scattered throughout your hometown and gather them to rebuild your project.<p></p>\n<p>Along the way, you’ll come across the wayward townsfolk who have found the pieces of your project before you. Barter with, trade for, and trap them with whatever you can find to get those pieces back. One man’s trash is another’s treasure, after all!</p>\n<p>Oh, and take care to search everything thoroughly. An old town like this can hide many secrets.</p>\n<p>By any chance, you wouldn’t have happened to hear that whispering, did you?</p>\n<p><b>Game Features</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Easy mouse gameplay for clicking and dragging. The only keyboard inputs are ESC to leave the game.\n</li><li>Five areas to explore filled with interactive animations.\n</li><li>Inventory system to store and combine items.\n</li><li>Animated replayable cutscenes and dialogue with new and fan-favorite characters.\n</li><li>Four minigames and minigame variants.\n</li><li>Postgame content (sshhhh…..)\n</li></ul>\n",
